        "titulo": "Review: direct object pronouns",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: forms: «mi, ti, lo/la, ci, vi, li/le». STEP 2: position: before the conjugated verb, after «non», attached to an infinitive and to «ecco». STEP 3: before a vowel, «lo» and «la» shorten to «l'». STEP 4: in the passato prossimo with «avere», the participle agrees with «lo, la, li, le». STEP 5: verbs such as «cercare», «ascoltare», «aspettare» and «chiamare» take a direct object.",
        "comparacao": "The two big changes from English are word order and agreement. If you put the pronoun in the right place (before a conjugated verb, attached to an infinitive) and, in the passato prossimo, give the participle the ending of «lo, la, li, le», the sentence is right.",
